 "_comment": "General solubility rules (src/solubility.rs, `insoluble_by_rules`): the fallback that says whether a cation-anion pair without a tabulated Ksp and without formation data forms an insoluble solid. Textbook rules (alkali metals, ammonium and H+ give soluble salts; nitrates, acetates, perchlorates soluble; halides soluble except Ag, Pb, Hg(I), Cu(I), Tl; sulfates except Ba, Sr, Pb, Ca, Ag; hydroxides, sulfides, carbonates, phosphates mostly insoluble ...). mode: never | always | only (insoluble with the listed cations, optionally with every group-2 cation or every cation of charge >= 3) | except (insoluble with every cation but the listed ones, optionally also not with group 2). An anion with no rule forms no solid. Tier Speculative.",
